# Kinetum Private Validation Kit @KINETUM_VERSION@

Internal integration and CloudLab tools for an independently installed runtime.
Install this private Python wheel with pip into the operator's chosen environment.

## Preparation

Use the existing configured platform build directory; `build` below is the
name chosen when running `cmake -S . -B build`. The command
`cmake --build build --target kinetum_validation_kit` packages the compiled
helpers, rebuilding them only if needed, and stages the kit beneath that same
directory. It creates no second platform build. On x86-64 the result is
`build/kinetum_validation-@KINETUM_VERSION@-py3-none-linux_x86_64.whl`;
the AArch64 build produces the corresponding `linux_aarch64.whl`.
Its native helpers target the build host architecture; use the matching
native build for the validation machine. Documentation rendering and release
signing are not prerequisites for this target.

On the prepared Linux lab host, install the transferred wheel into a Python
environment outside the runtime prefix. This x86-64 example creates that
environment at `/var/tmp/kinetum-validation`:

```bash
python3 -B -m venv /var/tmp/kinetum-validation
/var/tmp/kinetum-validation/bin/python3 -B -m pip install ./kinetum_validation-@KINETUM_VERSION@-py3-none-linux_x86_64.whl
```

## Running

```bash
sudo /var/tmp/kinetum-validation/bin/python3 -I -B -X utf8 -m kinetum_validation --runtime-root /opt/kinetum --test-type standard
sudo /var/tmp/kinetum-validation/bin/python3 -I -B -X utf8 -m kinetum_benchmark run --runtime-root /opt/kinetum --runs 30
/var/tmp/kinetum-validation/bin/python3 -I -B -X utf8 -m kinetum_benchmark report --input-dir /tmp/kinetum_benchmark
```

Python 3.12 or newer is required locally. The remote traffic endpoint retains
its independent interpreter setting. Run commands require an explicit runtime;
reporting consumes recorded artifacts and does not require a runtime root.
The installed `kinetum_validation/data/` directory supplies the default
`--validation-root`, which may also be selected explicitly. Runtime and
validation resource roots must be disjoint. Pip installs declared Python
dependencies, including Matplotlib; system tools remain host prerequisites.

Before run metadata or traffic setup, the harness executes the protected
runtime's `kinetum-info --check --json` and admits its verified metadata.
Runtime, kit, and information-image versions must agree. No compatibility subset or
additional kit attestation is involved.

Hugepage and TRex helpers remain explicit lab-owner actions. Runtime binaries,
module/provider images, source-build dependency production, and documentation
build tools are not contained here. Apache-2.0 terms, the Kinetum notice, and
kit-specific third-party notices are included with the package resources.
